    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Pagan Lithuanian dukes, united after their victory at Saule in 1236, built one of the largest states of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>Ruled by the Gediminid dynasty, it absorbed much of Rus' and used Ruthenian as its chancery language.</li><li>Joined to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#poland">Poland</a> from 1386 and in the Commonwealth from 1569, it was partitioned, mostly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#russia">Russia</a>, by 1795.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#lithuania">Lithuania</a> was the last pagan state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>: its official conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#catholicism">Catholicism</a> began only in 1387, and that of Samogitia not until 1413.</p></aside>
    </section>

